From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <engineering@projectluma.org>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] lumaui: Sound › Volume mixer as playing rows

The Volume mixer (sound-mixer) is drawn from what is playing instead of a
grid of channel strips. The hero is the Sound page's: a tile per output of
org.projectluma.AudioDevices1 (label, detail and a glyph by kind), four to
a line and wrapping, the default one raised; a press makes another the
default through the sound adapter's out key (CFSINKS now maps a node name
to that key's id). Under them the output's volume and its level in the
slider's column: a LumaAudioMeter without zones, 32 segments 5 px tall,
3 px apart and 2 px round.

Playing now is a Settings group with a LumaUI LumaMediaRow per listed
app: artwork and badge, title, "App · artist" or "App · Paused at 14:02",
the transport the player offers, volume, mute, a 28-segment level, and the
output picker (LumaUI's menu on the row's chip: the main output first,
then every output; raised while the app is sent elsewhere). Other sounds
are Settings slider rows in the same kind of group for the entries the
service marks other (System sounds, Phone). Their sliders are 180 px
where the row has room (140 on a phone) and shrink below that, so a narrow
window still reaches its phone layout. An icon the service gives as a
file is drawn with the Settings row image, as a fixture's artwork is. Without a listed app there is no Playing now
card. Apps that are not listed, and "Default" under an app, are gone.

Up and Down move from one volume to the next. Volume writes keep one call
per app in flight. Levels are watched for the listed apps and the output
only while the page is mapped in a window that is not suspended.

The page needs the service at version 3 and shows its unavailable state
below that. Sound's row is always Volume mixer; the adapter's mixer flag
and its proxy go. The fixture lists the page (54 pages), and a fixture
that carries CFMIX (the service's outputs, applications and levels as
JSON) is drawn from it without the bus.
